<header><p class="st-kicker">other · Caucasus</p><h1 class="st-title">Baku Commune</h1><p class="st-meta">1918 CE – 1918 CE · capital Baku</p></header>
<p class="st-teaser">A Bolshevik-led government that ruled Baku for a few months in 1918 and whose leaders became Soviet martyrs as the 26 Baku Commissars.</p>
<div class="st-body"><div class="st-text"><h2>Origins</h2><p>In March 1918 the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/baku">Baku</a> Soviet, dominated by <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/communist-party-of-the-soviet-union">Bolsheviks</a> and supported by <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/armenian-revolutionary-federation">Armenian Dashnak</a> forces, defeated Azerbaijani <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/musavat">Musavat</a> units in fighting known as the March Days, in which thousands of Muslims were killed. In April it formed the Baku <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/council-of-peoples-commissars">Council of People's Commissars</a> under <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/stepan-shaumian">Stepan Shaumian</a>, part of the <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/empire/russian-sfsr">Russian SFSR</a>.</p><h2>Rule and society</h2><p>The Commune nationalised the oil industry and the Caspian fleet and tried to supply <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/empire/russian-sfsr">Soviet Russia</a> with oil. Its forces were mostly Armenian, and it was opposed by the Azerbaijani population. It faced an advance on <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/baku">Baku</a> by the Ottoman-led <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/caucasus-army-of-islam">Army of Islam</a>, which defeated its troops in June and July 1918.</p><h2>Decline and legacy</h2><p>On 31 July 1918 the Commune resigned after the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/baku">Baku</a> Soviet voted to invite British help, and the <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/state/centrocaspian-dictatorship">Centrocaspian Dictatorship</a> took over. Its leaders fled, were captured and shot near <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/turkmenbasy">Krasnovodsk</a> in September 1918, becoming the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/26-baku-commissars">26 Baku Commissars</a> of Soviet legend.</p></div><aside class="st-side"><figure class="st-fig"><img src="/images/states/baku-commune.jpg" alt="Baku Commune" width="320" height="240"><figcaption>Image: Неизвестный художник (не указан в выходных данных плаката; отсутствует авторская монограмма или подпись) · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:%D0%9C%D1%8B_%D0%BD%D0%B8%D0%BA%D0%BE%D0%B3%D0%B4%D0%B0_%D0%BD%D0%B5_%D0%B7%D0%B0%D0%B1%D1%83%D0%B4%D0%B5%D0%BC_26_%D1%83%D0%B1%D0%B8%D1%82%D1%8B%D1%85_%D0%B0%D0%BD%D0%B3%D0%BB%D0%B8%D0%B9%D1%81%D0%BA%D0%B8%D0%BC%D0%B8_%D0%B8%D0%BC%D0%BF%D0%B5%D1%80%D0%B8%D0%B0%D0%BB%D0%B8%D1%81%D1%82%D0%B0%D0%BC%D0%B8.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">source</a></figcaption></figure><dl class="st-facts"><dt>Years</dt><dd>1918 CE – 1918 CE</dd><dt>Century</dt><dd><a href="/centuries/20th-century">20th century</a></dd><dt>Type</dt><dd>other</dd><dt>Character</dt><dd>bureaucratic</dd><dt>Capital</dt><dd>Baku</dd><dt>Rulers</dt><dd>Stepan Shaumian</dd><dt>Language</dt><dd>Russian</dd><dt>Today</dt><dd><a href="/countries/azerbaijan">Azerbaijan</a></dd><dt>Also</dt><dd>Baku Soviet, Baku Council of People's Commissars</dd></dl><figure class="st-locator"><a href="/atlas?year=1918&amp;focus=baku-commune" aria-label="Baku Commune on the atlas"><svg class="map map-loc" viewBox="5904 735 640 512" role="img" aria-label="Map: where Baku Commune lay"><image href="/maps/world.svg" x="0" y="0" width="10000" height="4393"/><path class="map-tie" d="M6224 991L5820 533M6224 991L6224 991"/><path class="map-dot-n" d="M5820 533h0M6224 991h0"/><path class="map-dot-halo" d="M6224 991h0"/><path class="map-dot-me" d="M6224 991h0"/></svg></a><figcaption>The dot marks Baku. <a href="/atlas?year=1918&amp;focus=baku-commune">On the atlas &rarr;</a></figcaption></figure></aside></div>
